.TH "m2_ (1)" "" "October 2026" "" ""
.SH NAME
m2_ \- a \f[I]BASH\f[R] script that loads and executes functions from
another script.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[CR]m2_\f[R] \-h
.PP
\f[CR]m2_\f[R] [options] [ \f[CR]\-\-\-\f[R] ] command
[x\-options|sub\-command]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]m2_\f[R] is a utility script that is used as the target of a link
to a \f[I]derivative\f[R] script.
That derivative script when run will then load a library file and run
functions within it.
.PP
The \f[CR]m2_\f[R] script itself provides much of the infrastructure
that one would want a utility script to have.
.PP
The derivative script will support the commands that \f[I]m2_\f[R]
provides.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-O arg\f[R]
Output file, \f[CR]d_output=arg\f[R]
.TP
\f[CR]\-P arg\f[R]
password, \f[CR]d_password=arg\f[R]
.TP
\f[CR]\-a\f[R]
alternative flag, \f[CR]d_aflag=yes\f[R]
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R]
help flag, \f[CR]d_helpflag=yes\f[R]
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R]
quiet flag, \f[CR]d_quiet=yes\f[R]
.TP
